      "content": "Small UI cleanup requested: the view switcher in the board toolbar must stop showing the numeric count badges next to the \"Board\" and \"Table\" labels.\n\nFile: src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue\n\nCurrent behaviour\n- The `viewTabs` computed (in the <script> block) returns objects with a `count` value, and the template renders it as a `badge badge-xs` inside each switcher button:\n    { id: 'board',  label: 'Board',  icon: 'fa-solid fa-columns',     count: this.sidebarTasks.length }\n    { id: 'table',  label: 'Table',  icon: 'fa-solid fa-table-list',  count: this.boardChats.length }\n  Sprint branch:\n    { id: 'board',  ..., count: this.totalTasks }\n    { id: 'table',  ..., count: this.totalTasks }\n\nRequested change (default scope, keep it minimal)\n1. In the `viewTabs` computed, remove the `count` property from the `board` and `table` entries only \u2014 both in the `isSprintBoard` branch and in the kanban branch. Do NOT touch the Planning / Follow-up entries (their counts stay) nor the `gantt` entry (already `count: null`).\n2. Leave the template badge block (`<span v-if=\"tab.count != null\" ...>{{ tab.count }}</span>`) untouched: with no `count` on board/table it simply does not render, and Planning/Follow-up keep working.\n3. No other behaviour change: do not remove the `sidebarTasks` / `boardChats` / `totalTasks` computeds (they are still used elsewhere, e.g. the \"N columns \u00b7 N tasks\" subtitle and the stats panel).\n\nAcceptance criteria\n- Board and Table buttons in the toolbar show only icon + label, with no number badge, for both kanban and sprint boards.\n- Planning and Follow-up buttons keep their counts; Gantt unchanged.\n- No console warnings, no unused-variable/ESLint errors introduced, component still switches views normally.\n- Diff is limited to src/components/kanban/board/KanbanBoardView.vue.",
